A nested loop here would be O(3,000 × 3,000) = up to 9 million string comparisons per import. That's not catastrophic for a single CPU-bound operation on its own, but it's wasteful, and Apex transactions have a 10-second CPU limit that this transaction shares with the rest of the import job (DML, triggers, other logic). A single `Map<String, Id>` built from `contacts` in one pass, then a single lookup per lead, is O(n + m), far safer against CPU timeouts, and arguably just as readable. I'd do it that way instead of the nested loop.

